  "goodToKnow": "Das Massaker is a massacre: ein Massaker an der Zivilbevölkerung. It's neuter in German, and the plural is the same. Massakrieren means to massacre. In German remembrance culture, massacres committed by the Wehrmacht and SS, such as in Oradour-sur-Glane (France, 1944) or Lidice (Czechoslovakia, 1942), are commemorated, often with visits by German presidents. From French massacre."
